### InverSeek Indexing Service - runnable HTTP checks
### Book 1342 must have been ingested first. Expected results are in the comments.
@base = http://localhost:7002

### Health -> 200 {"service":"indexing","status":"UP",...}
GET {{base}}/health

### Index one ingested book -> 200 {"book_id":1342,"index":"updated"}
POST {{base}}/index/update/1342

### Same book again (idempotent) -> 200, same postings
POST {{base}}/index/update/1342

### Book without completion marker -> 404 {"error":"book_not_found"}
POST {{base}}/index/update/9999999

### Invalid id -> 400 {"error":"invalid_book_id"}
POST {{base}}/index/update/abc

### Status -> 200 {"books_indexed":N,"last_update":"...","index_size_MB":N,"index_version":N}
GET {{base}}/index/status

### Reindex every ingested book, one publication per book -> 200 {"total":N,"indexed":N,"failed":0}
POST {{base}}/index

### Replace the whole index atomically -> 200 {"books_processed":N,"elapsed_time":"..."}
POST {{base}}/index/rebuild
